# Cloudflare Pages runs `npx @cloudflare/next-on-pages@1` to build this
# project. Since wrangler 4.129.0 (and @cloudflare/workers-types 5.x,
# published 2026-09-03) that install fails to resolve:
#
#   Found: @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260702.1
#     peerOptional @cloudflare/workers-types@"^4.20240208.0"
#       from @cloudflare/next-on-pages@1.13.16
#   Could not resolve:
#     peerOptional @cloudflare/workers-types@"^5.20260903.1"
#       from wrangler@4.129.0
#
# next-on-pages pulls wrangler ^4 as a peer, but pins workers-types to ^4,
# and wrangler has since moved to ^5 — an upstream conflict we can't fix
# from here. next-on-pages is deprecated in favour of the OpenNext adapter,
# so a fixed release is unlikely.
#
# npm's own error names the remedy ("retry this command with --force or
# --legacy-peer-deps"). This is the same pre-npm-7 resolution behaviour, and
# it only relaxes PEER ranges — direct dependencies still resolve exactly as
# the lockfile says.
#
# Migrating to the OpenNext Cloudflare adapter would remove the need for
# this; see https://opennext.js.org/cloudflare
legacy-peer-deps=true
